ultramodern: say what the video interface will show next

A caller driving a game wants the frame the game has just finished, and the
registers a screen update carries are not it. A retrace posts the registers it
is about to replace and then swaps: the frame on them is the one the interface
was already showing, and the game's newest frame -- handed over with
osViSwapBuffer and waiting for the retrace that shows it -- is one behind. For a
game that has gone quiet between frames, which is exactly when a gym reads it,
that is always one frame of lag.

`update_vi` already works the right registers out of the next VI state before it
swaps. That part is now `next_regs`, and `next_vi_regs` returns what it makes
without swapping anything: the origin, width, vertical window, scale and status
the next retrace will scan out with. `update_vi` does exactly what it did.

